    "notes": "The actual named principal-shrine platform and four independently mapped body/roof/finial records retain raw east/south positions. The shrine grid is37.6656 degrees south of east; all four door faces remain symmetric. The small platform top clears standard terrain samples within its mapped footprint, with50cm foundation depth beneath corner samples. No ground or water excavation is requested. Full-site loading replaces five records and preserves1612 independent buildings in the960m tile exactly. Three native water features retain57903.0123 square metres. Failure keeps all1617 native buildings; eviction preserves both surfaces and frees model geometry. A synthetic16m partial tile retains original terrain beneath and around clipped model pieces. Its empty semantic context proves clipping/lifecycle only; temporary cut faces are not permanent temple geometry."
