    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Accepted for the specific principal Pashupatinath pagoda exterior and approximate normal-map/DEM fit. The two roof footprints and upper-storey plan are mapped controls; nominal heights and the23.07m tip combine normal-map tags with ordinary picture/article guidance. Upper roof pitch, individual struts, timber bands, silver door panels, finial beads and foundation thresholds are visualization estimates. The broader precinct, eastern gate, separate pavilions, river shrines and ghats remain independent context; they are not merged into the principal shrine model. No claim is made for exact carvings, deity figures, navigable interiors or surveyed archaeological thresholds. No bespoke survey or archival reconstruction research was used."
